{"id": "EUVD-2026-101075", "enisaUuid": "92be3e0d-ff73-3a7f-8896-5b3637a7db4e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mwifiex: fix IRQ leak using wrong index in MSI-X error path\n\nmwifiex_pcie_request_irq() registers each MSI-X vector with a per-index\ndev_id (&card->msix_ctx[i]). On a request_irq() failure the cleanup loop\n\"for (j = 0; j < i; j++)\" frees msix_entries[j].vector but passes the\nfailed index's &card->msix_ctx[i] as the dev_id. free_irq() matches on\n(irq, dev_id), so it fails to find the action registered with\n&card->msix_ctx[j]: the already-requested IRQ j is not freed (leaked) and\nfree_irq() warns about freeing a non-existent IRQ. Use &card->msix_ctx[j].", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:20", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/11bc2cbb14f450eaa47cce9eb086f948ef8f4bcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a60cb2292194cc9eafae7ca8a8a72d37ae78d97", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fcac5813f324cd07dfd36b4adf624fc70f7587d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2761b21cb896b1da8dd46cee5084c9032b2d7098", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fd4cc87e6cc0839aac89c24ebe39ce262fe088f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0969c9688389f2e0f65b1a924b0dd6625a3bb776", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03d5e4776e8b71c2468c5c3c48b39202c87a8796", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a3d722190cdef18da4878b5efc27c3c386dda248"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98426", "GHSA-558r-qp8j-rr6r"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1862e2eb-8122-38cc-b322-8a71aec594e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1b96123c-d492-3091-9397-1c552fe2466d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3a0e71b6-e3e1-3580-be23-ffead87244d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "99074fc1e67b374b5c72406a2